b9e4a8daf6"}, "language": "english", "review": "I don't play this game just because of the TF2 hat, its a great game!", "timestamp_created": 1550367141, "timestamp_updated": 1550367141, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.485074609518051147", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "49031770", "author": {"steamid": "76561198015003424", "personaname": "Nucular", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/NucularS/", "num_games_owned": 1509, "num_reviews": 394, "playtime_forever": 2225, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2225, "last_played": 1550263744, "avatar": "57fd6389fb776061ca96a627ea8cd1fcb481549e"}, "language": "english", "review": "Alien Swarm is a great top-down alien coop shooter or at least a great base for one. Unfortunately, it has always felt more like someone's side project than a real Valve game seeing as how there is a single campaign consisting of six missions, barely tied together by a thin veneer of a story, Left 4 Dead style, and the game has never received much support since release. Surprisingly, there are still a couple of people playing online at any given time, so it is still possible to find someone to play with, even if Alien Swarm: Reactive Drop makes the original title somewhat obsolete with new campaigns, more settings, and fixes for many outstanding issues. The remake is not a Valve release, but I would argue that the community has done a far better job. On the other side, the remake did not seem to have anyone playing, so you might be better off playing the original, unless you have someone to play with.", "timestamp_created": 1550329113, "timestamp_updated": 1550329113, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.5181714892